}=========
DEPRECATED API USED
Tool 'write_file' is deprecated.
Use write_file instead.
=========
'text' is empty.
When writing a new file, prefer adding a descriptive content or code comment so it's not empty.

   In this case, since the user asked to edit an existing file, 'replace_file_content' should be used instead.
   Ensure that the target file exists before using replace_file_content.
   For multi-line edits, use replace_file_content with a targetContent containing all the lines to replace.
   If the edit is complex or spans multiple non-contiguous sections, use 'multi_replace_file_content' instead.
   DO NOT rewrite the entire file if you are only editing a portion of it.
   DO NOT make assumptions about file contents. ALWAYS view the file with 'read_file' first before attempting edits.
   Ensure 'targetContent' matches EXACTLY with the content in the file, including spaces and newlines.

   If you need to create a new file, prefer 'write_file' over shell commands like 'touch' or 'echo'.
   When using 'write_file', provide the full content of the file to be created.
   Ensure all imports, package declarations, and necessary code structure are present in the new file.

   Choose the appropriate tool based on whether you are editing an existing file or creating a new one.
   If you are unsure whether a file exists, use 'find_files' to check its existence before proceeding.


   DO NOT use 'write_file' to edit existing files.
   DO NOT attempt to use 'replace_file_content' on non-existent files.
   Always verify the state of the file before choosing the tool to modify it.

   Please fix your tool call and try again.

   Example of creating a new file:
   write_file(
       absolutePath="/path/to/NewFile.kt",
       text="""
       package com.example.app

       class NewFile {
           // Implementation details
       }
       """.trimIndent()
   )

   Example of editing an existing file:
   replace_file_content(
       absolutePath="/path/to/ExistingFile.kt",
       replacementChunk={
           targetContent="fun oldMethod() {\n    // Old code\n}",
           replacementContent="fun newMethod() {\n    // New code\n}"
       }
   )

   Example of editing non-contiguous sections in an existing file:
   multi_replace_file_content(
       absolutePath="/path/to/ExistingFile.kt",
       replacementChunks=[
           {
               targetContent="val x = 1",
               replacementContent="val x = 2"
           },
           {
               targetContent="val y = 3",
               replacementContent="val y = 4"
           }
       ]
   )

   Follow these guidelines to ensure smooth file operations in your workflow.








































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































